      {
        "title": "Show HN: NES Contra (1987) port (ASM –> C and then C –> WebAssembly)",
        "link": "https://epoyraz.github.io/nes-contra-us/",
        "description": "<p>Based on vermiceli's annotated disassembly of Contra: <a href=\"https://github.com/vermiceli/nes-contra-us\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://github.com/vermiceli/nes-contra-us</a>. Thanks for the great work.<p>I ported it in two steps. First to C: the game logic is translated routine by routine from the 6502 assembly, and checked frame by frame against the original in the Mesen emulator. Then the C code to WebAssembly so it runs in the browser.<p>The cherry on top: online multiplayer, so two players can play co-op over the internet.<p>Source: <a href=\"https://github.com/epoyraz/nes-contra-us\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://github.com/epoyraz/nes-contra-us</a></p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50319169\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50319169</a></p>\n<p>Points: 77</p>\n<p># Comments: 46</p>",
